# Keep the landing page current

The README is the status page, and `web/` (redlamp.app) presents it. When you update the README for something that landed, check the site in the same change.

## Updates itself (don't duplicate)

- **Roadmap** and **Everything that works today** are parsed from the README at build time by `web/lib/readme.ts`. Each roadmap item's state (done, in progress, not started) and each phase's tracked-work counts come from the tracker rows the item names (`web/lib/tracker.ts`).
- **The Compare page** (`/compare`) and the comparison summary under the roadmap are read from `docs/lightroom-comparison.md` (`web/lib/comparison.ts`); its tracker IDs link to their GitHub issues (`trackerIssues` in `web/lib/github.ts`). Keep it in step with `.cursor/rules/roadmap-and-comparison.mdc`.
- **The Performance page** (`/performance`) and the home page's performance strip are read from `docs/performance/metrics.json` and `history.jsonl` (`web/lib/performance.ts`); `scripts/perf-record.sh` adds a run, as `.cursor/rules/performance.mdc` describes.
- **The Cameras page** (`/cameras`) is read from `docs/cameras.md` (`web/lib/cameras.ts`), whose lists `scripts/camera-list.py` generates from the decode tests (`tests/decode/cameras.json`), the sample downloads (`mise run fixtures`, `fixtures-shoots`, the look-development manifest) and the vendored LibRaw's camera list. When you add a sample to the decode tests or update LibRaw, run `scripts/camera-list.py --apply` (with LibRaw's source in `vendor/cache`, from `scripts/vendor-libraw.sh`) and commit `docs/cameras.md`; the pre-commit hook, `mise run lint` and CI check it. Only the text above its generated block is written by hand.
- **Screenshots, film icons, sample sheets and logos** are copied from `docs/` by `web/scripts/sync-assets.mjs`.
- **The download button**, the version in the hero's status pill and the Homebrew "(with the first release)" note follow the latest GitHub release (`web/lib/github.ts`).

Keep the shapes the parsers rely on, or update them:
- `## Roadmap` with `### Phase N: Title *(status)*` sections and `- [x]` / `- [ ]` items (`### Later` uses plain `-` items), each ending in `<!-- tracker: ID, ID -->` or `<!-- internal -->` where it has them.
- `### What works today` with `**Group title**` lines, each followed by `- [x]` items.
- `docs/lightroom-comparison.md`: `## Group` headings, each with a table of Feature, Lightroom, Redlamp, vs Lightroom, Phase, Tracker and Notes, in the vocabulary the document defines.

## Edit by hand when the README changes

| README change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| A headline feature lands, or a feature row's claims change | The matching entry in `web/content/features.ts` (title, body, points, screenshot) |
| The command palette's keys or behaviour change | `commandPalette` and `paletteSteps` in `web/content/features.ts`, and its close-ups (`palette-*` in `scripts/capture-screenshots.sh`) |
| A new cut of the film is published | `film` in `web/lib/site.ts` (YouTube ID, link, duration), its poster in `web/public/video`, and the README's link under the hero |
| The editor's look changes (panels, layout, the default theme), or a hero shot's feature does | The hero shots: `scripts/capture-hero.sh <photo folder>` regenerates `docs/images/hero*.png`, which the README and `heroShots` in `web/content/features.ts` show, with their captions |
| Measured performance numbers change | Record a run (`scripts/perf-record.sh`); the speed feature's points in `web/content/features.ts` are written by hand |
| The number of keyboard shortcuts changes | The develop feature's points in `web/content/features.ts` |
| A film stock is added, renamed or re-tuned | `web/content/films.ts` (with its icon and `look-<id>.jpg` in `docs/images/film/`) |
| Goals change | `principles` in `web/content/features.ts` |
| Status changes (alpha, beta, iPad/iPhone) | `status`, `stage` (the status badge) and `homebrew` in `web/lib/site.ts`, and the hero copy in `web/components/sections/Hero.tsx`. A new stage also changes the version suffix in `Version.xcconfig` (`-prealpha`, `-alpha`, `-beta`) |
| A new screenshot is added to `docs/images` | Use it in a feature row or add it to `gallery` in `web/content/features.ts` |
| An AI feature lands or changes models, or how agents build Redlamp changes (`AGENTS.md`, waves, the agent recipe studio, CI) | `aiDisclosure` in `web/content/ai.ts` |
| A release ships something worth announcing in the app | A highlight in `web/content/whats-new/<id>/` for that version, at most four per release (`web/README.md`, What's New) |

Write site copy in the brand voice from `docs/brand/README.md`: calm, plain and precise, with no exclamation marks or superlatives, and only claims the README makes.

## Check

```bash
scripts/roadmap-sync.py --check
scripts/camera-list.py --check
cd web && npm test && npm run typecheck && npm run build
```

The build fails if the README sections the parser needs are missing, or if a comparison row breaks the document's vocabulary.
